NAVER Corporation has modified this binary.

Six bytes at file offset 0x426e6 were overwritten with NOP
instructions, neutralising a single unsigned-greater conditional branch
in ExternalCameraDeviceSession::configureV4l2StreamLocked().  The
branch rejected V4L2 buffer sizes larger than width * height * 2, which
several UVC camera firmwares over-report by a constant metadata
padding, leaving those cameras with no usable stream.

  before: 0f 87 ba 01 00 00      ; ja  <error>
  after:  90 90 90 90 90 90      ; 6 x nop

No other byte of the file was changed; the GNU build-ID, .dynsym and
every other code path are byte-identical to the upstream LineageOS
20.0 build.  The full rationale and the disassembly of the affected
hot path are recorded in the package's ebuild.

  MD5 unmodified : 2b2b0a73e12e0083f684496f224d54b0
  MD5 modified   : 4971b50f4e9d02b11de71637c9a2fabc

